# ---- Node / Vite (frontend, T-004) ----
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# `backend/openapi.json` and `frontend/src/api/schema.d.ts` are generated and **committed**
# on purpose (T-405). Committing them means `npm run build` needs no Python, and a developer
# who changed a route without regenerating sees a dirty working tree — which, with no CI in
# this repo, is the only signal there is. A backend pytest guards the first against the app.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ---- Data / runtime artifacts ----
*.log
/tmp/
minio-data/
# Local-filesystem object-storage backend (STORAGE_BACKEND=local, T-201)
.data/
pgdata/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---- Private to this working copy (not published) ----
# Third-party / course-supplied source material — not ours to relicense under GPL-3.0.
ReferenceDocs/
RAG Chatbot GUI Design/
# Internal build board and phase plan.
planning/
# Authoritative specification (requirement IDs, rulings, open issues).
Nexus_AI_Detailed_Specification.md
# Agent orientation + project skills (reference the excluded docs above).
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# ---- Third-party OAuth credentials (NEVER commit) ----
# Google Cloud Console hands you a `client_secret_*.json` containing a live
# `GOCSPX-` secret. Corpus needs it in **Keycloak only** (R-63: the backend stores no
# third-party credential), so the file has no business in this tree at all — this is a
# backstop for the window between downloading it and moving it somewhere safe.
client_secret_*.json
*client_secret*.json
credentials.json

